Suggests: esemnbun-cli
Description: sign and verify documents with the Moldovan eID card (GNOME app)
 eSemnBun signs documents with the qualified certificate on the Moldovan
 electronic identity card (IDEMIA CosmoX ID-A) through a USB smart-card
 reader, and verifies signed documents offline.
 .
  * PDF documents are signed as PAdES-T, accepted by msign.gov.md
  * other files are signed as detached XAdES (BES, T or C)
  * browser connection compatible with the MoldSign Desktop protocol,
    with consent before every signature
  * the PIN can be remembered in the Secret Service (GNOME Keyring), per card
 .
 The reader is reached through pcscd (CCID readers via libccid).

Package: esemnbun-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         pcscd,
         libccid,
         libpcsclite1,
         libssl3t64 | libssl3
Description: sign and verify documents with the Moldovan eID card (command line)
 The `esemnbun` command signs PDF (PAdES-T) and other files (XAdES), verifies
 signatures offline, reads the card certificate, and runs the browser bridge
 (MoldSign Server protocol on localhost) for msign.gov.md.
 .
 Ships a systemd user unit, esemnbun-server.service, which is not enabled
 by default: systemctl --user enable --now esemnbun-server.service
